<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Smithsonian</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Smithsonian Institution is a group of museums and research centres in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/washington-dc">Washington, D.C.</a> Its collections have included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-bronzes">Benin Bronzes</a> looted by British forces in 1897. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a> list it among the institutions involved in the debate over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/repatriation-of-cultural-property">restitution</a> of these objects.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/smithsonian.jpg" alt="Smithsonian" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nate Lee · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smithsonian_Building_Sunlight.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
